Three manuscript editions of his writings and translations were deposited respectively in rNgog Blo ldan shes rab's tomb, in the monastery of gSang phu (probably in the main assembly hall), and in Drin las kyi sde (ID:4357) ([7FZ3B926]: 107).</note></person><person xml:id="person3892"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sa skya paN+Di ta kun dga' rgyal mtshan</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ས་སྐྱ་པཎྜི་ཏ་ཀུན་དགའ་རྒྱལ་མཚན</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sa skya paṇḍita</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos rje sa paN</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos rje</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">chos kyi rje</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">rigs gter gangs can mkhas pa'i gtsug rgyan</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sa paN</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sa skya lo tsA ba</persName><birth notBefore="1182-01-01" notAfter="1182-12-31">1182</birth><death notBefore="1251-01-01" notAfter="1251-12-31">1251</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1056</idno><idno type="APIS">3892</idno><note type="comment">See [8S7FDMCJ]: 107 for a list of his most important disciples.</note></person><person xml:id="person3893"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jam dbyangs 'od zer mgon po</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">འཇམ་དབྱངས་འོད་ཟེར་མགོན་པོ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sgros snying pa 'od zer mgon po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sgros rnying pa 'od zer mgon po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mkhas pa 'od zer mgon po</persName><birth notBefore="1200-01-01">after 1200</birth><death notAfter="1350-12-31">before 1350</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P8LS14991</idno><idno type="APIS">3893</idno><note type="comment">Seventh abbot of gSang phu lower monastery. [D5VJHLSN]: 19 mentions two 'Od zer mgon po of gSang phu, the abbot, fl. mid-to-late 1200s, and the author of a work on the Perfection of wisdom, fl. late 13th-early 14th c.?.</note></person><person xml:id="person3894"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jam dbyangs shakya gzhon nu</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">འཇམ་དབྱངས་ཤཀྱ་གཞོན་ནུ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gsang phu shAkya gzhon nu</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">gsang phu mkhan po shAkya gzhon nu</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">'jam dbyangs shAkya gzhon nu</persName><birth notAfter="1270-12-31">before 1270</birth><death notBefore="1352-01-01">after 1352</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P5500</idno><idno type="APIS">3894</idno><note type="comment">Eighth throne-holder of gSang phu gling smad and 16th mkhan po of the Gling smad.&#13;
It is reported that during 'Jam dbyang Śākya gzhon nu's time as abbot of the sGros seminary of the Lower monastery (ca. 1326), there was a split between the old (rnying) and the new (gsar). Śākya gzhon nu's oral teachings were taught in "Old sGros" ([7FZ3B926]: 118).&#13;
This, however, conflicts with the dates determined for the dates of activity of the next abbot in [CCSBSVCA]: 686, namely 1293-1301.</note></person><person xml:id="person4024"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">grags pa rgya mtsho bde legs 'byung gnas</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">གྲགས་པ་རྒྱ་མཚོ་བདེ་ལེགས་འབྱུང་གནས</persName><birth notBefore="1200-01-01">after 1200</birth><death notAfter="1500-12-31">before 1500</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P3JT13458</idno><idno type="APIS">4024</idno><note type="comment">The closing verses mention 'Jam dbyangs 'od zer mgon po (ID:3893) as the source of the teaching - he could be 'Jam dbyangs shakya gzhon nu (ID:3894), the eighth abbot of the Lower monastery of gSang phu and founder of Tshal Gung thang. Possibly, the expression refers to both the eighth abbot ('jam dbyangs) and the seventh ('od zer mngon po).&#13;
See [J4L5X9AG]: 432, n. 58.</note></person><person xml:id="person5551"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">jñānaśrībhadra</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">ye shes dpal bzang po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">kha che dz+nya na shrI</persName><birth notBefore="1000-01-01">after 1000</birth><death notAfter="1100-12-31">before 1100</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P4CZ15186</idno><idno type="APIS">5551</idno><note type="comment">Approximate life dates: 11th century (see [AAIEJBMW]).</note></person><person xml:id="person5552"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">śaṅkaranandana</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bram ze shang ka ra nanda</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bram ze chen po</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bde byed ga' ba</persName><birth notBefore="0910-01-01" notAfter="0920-12-31">after 910 before 920</birth><death notBefore="0980-01-01" notAfter="0985-12-31">after 980 before 985</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P9952</idno><idno type="APIS">5552</idno><note type="comment">Dates 910/920-980/985 according to [XHAZ854J]: 354.&#13;
Other proposed dates are 940-1030, 940/950-1020/1030 (see [AAIEJBMW]).</note></person><person xml:id="person6418"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">śākyaśrībhadra</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">kha che paN chen</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">kha che paNDita</persName><birth notBefore="1127-01-01" notAfter="1127-12-31">1127</birth><death notBefore="1225-01-01" notAfter="1225-12-31">1225</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Indic</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1518</idno><idno type="APIS">6418</idno></person><person xml:id="person6604"><persName type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">nor bu bzang po</persName><persName xml:lang="bo">ནོར་བུ་བཟང་པོ</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">nor bu bzang po dpal</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">nor bzangs dpal</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">nor bzang dpal</persName><persName type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">mkhas pa nor bzang dpal</persName><birth notBefore="1300-01-01" notAfter="1320-12-31">after 1300 before 1320</birth><death notAfter="1400-12-31">afer 1315 before 1400</death><sex value="M"/><nationality>Tibetan</nationality><idno type="BDRC">https://purl.bdrc.io/resource/P1879</idno><idno type="APIS">6604</idno><note type="comment">See [4G8T8CP3].&#13;
According to [PSQXSBDP]: 107, 14th-century Sa skya pa scholar (contra 13th-c. in [JZP4CZRX], bdr:P1879).</note></person></listPerson><listBibl><bibl xml:id="work3774"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">pramāṇaviniścaya</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma rnam par nges pa</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma rnam nges</title><date type="composition" notBefore="0560-01-01" notAfter="0660-12-31">after 560 before 660</date><author ref="person:3773">dharmakīrti</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><idno type="APIS">3774</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work4785"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma rnam par nges pa'i sbyor 'phreng yid bzhin nor bu</title><title xml:lang="bo">ཚད་མ་རྣམ་པར་ངེས་པའི་སྦྱོར་འཕྲེང་ཡིད་བཞིན་ནོར་བུ</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma rnam par nges kyi 'grel ba</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma rnam par nges pa'i sbyor phreng yid bzhin nor bu</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">don gsal byed kyi me long</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">don gsal byed kyi me long</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sbyor ba nor bu'i 'phreng ba</title><title type="alt" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sbyor ba yid bzhin nor bu'i 'phreng ba</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1219-01-01">after 1219</date><author ref="person:4024">grags pa rgya mtsho bde legs 'byung gnas</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">Commentary on the PVin providing a summary of perception and inference at the beginning. &#13;
The chapter colophons give the tilte "don gsal byed kyi me long."&#13;
Composed after 1219, as it cites the Tshad ma rigs gter (ID:5564) several times.&#13;
Extensive use of chains of consequences.</note><relatedItem type="commentaryOn" target="work:3774"/><relatedItem type="citesWork" target="work:5564"/><idno type="APIS">4785</idno></bibl><bibl xml:id="work5564"><title type="main" xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshad ma rigs gter</title><title xml:lang="bo">ཚད་མ་རིགས་གཏེར</title><textLang mainLang="bo"/><date type="composition" notBefore="1219-01-01" notAfter="1219-12-31">1219</date><author ref="person:3892">sa skya paN+Di ta kun dga' rgyal mtshan</author><note type="isExtant">True</note><note type="comment">On 1219 as the approximate date of composition, see [8S7FDMCJ]: 101 and 303, n. 293.</note><idno type="APIS">5564</idno></bibl></listBibl><listPlace><place xml:id="place5559"><placeName xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">bod</placeName><placeName xml:lang="bo">བོད</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">gangs ri'i khrod la kha ba can gyi ljongs</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">ri bo gangs can</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">gangs ri'i khrod</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">gangs can</placeName><idno type="APIS">5559</idno></place><place xml:id="place5658"><placeName xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">tshal gung thang</placeName><placeName xml:lang="bo">ཚལ་གུང་ཐང</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">'tshal gung thang</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">tshal chos 'khor gling</placeName><location><geo>29.637434859197835 91.22657860776805</geo></location><idno type="APIS">5658</idno></place><place xml:id="place6043"><placeName xml:lang="bo-Latn-x-wylie">sgros rnying grwa tshang</placeName><placeName xml:lang="bo">སྒྲོས་རྙིང་གྲྭ་ཚང</placeName><placeName type="alt" xml:lang="bo">sgros snying</placeName><idno type="APIS">6043</idno></place></listPlace><listRelation><relation xml:id="rel2329" name="student-of" active="#person4024" passive="#person3893" type="positive"/><relation xml:id="rel2334" name="student-of" active="#person4024" passive="#person3894" type="uncertain